1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:19,620
Well, good morning, church.

2
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:23,480
Man, that was fun to sing that.

3
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:25,040
There's nothing better than you.

4
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:30,320
On our way in, Murs and I were listening to this other worship song about kind of a similar topic.

5
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:35,240
And he was talking about when God says to Israel not to have any other gods before me.

6
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:41,320
And he said, man, like, growing up, I always viewed that as, like, God was, like, you know, heavy-handed coming down.

7
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:43,400
Like, you can't worship any other gods before me.

8
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:49,240
He said, but as I grow in my faith, I learn to realize that God says that because he knows no other gods work.

9
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:50,080
Right?

10
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:54,500
He's saying, like, have no other gods before me because they don't work.

11
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:58,440
But how often, we can sing that over and over and over again, there's nothing better than you.

12
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:02,080
But how often do we live our lives as if there's a lot of other things better than God?

13
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:04,360
How often do we invest our time and our energy?

14
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:07,820
And so Sunday mornings are such a good reminder for all of us.

15
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:08,720
That's why we sing, right?

16
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:15,540
We sing to remind ourselves of truth that oftentimes we don't live as if it's true.

17
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:17,440
So, man, I needed that this morning.

18
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:21,120
Donovan, team, thanks so much for that encouragement this morning.

19
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:27,140
Last week, I talked from 2 Timothy about persevering trials.

20
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:35,720
And we were doing this series kind of called God Only Knows, where we're just week to week seeking God.

21
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:40,200
And, like, I think I confessed to some of you last week as a planner, like, that's a struggle for me.

22
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,280
I like to know where we're headed.

23
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:49,860
And so, man, as we have been talking about trials the last couple weeks, I just felt the Lord leading me to the book of James, which I'm really excited about.

24
00:01:49,860 --> 00:02:00,120
So, over the next few weeks, I don't know exactly how long it's going to take, but I just feel like led to hop into the book of James and talk about some things there.

25
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:05,980
And really, COVID, for all of us, has led us to different seasons of various trials.

26
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:14,360
As a country, as a community, as a church, as individuals, all of us throughout these past few years have faced different types of trials.

27
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:24,660
And maybe you're in here and you're not facing a trial, I would plead with you to look around your community and find ways to encourage others who are going through a difficult time.

28
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:35,780
So, I thought it would be good to kind of hop into the book of James, because we're going to see that the backdrop of the book of James is a group of people who are struggling, who are going through trials.

29
00:02:36,860 --> 00:02:45,640
But don't worry, if you're like Ryan, this is like week three of trials, and I don't come to church to be discouraged, I come to church to be encouraged.

30
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:51,500
If you're like Ryan, my social media feed is filled with trials and difficulty and bad news.

31
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:58,660
If your social media feed, if your news is anything like my news, it's filled with bad news, and you're like Ryan, three weeks of trials is enough.

32
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:06,400
I promise you, the book of James, the backdrop is trials, but the book of James is all about obedience, right?

33
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:16,520
It's about like us following God, us choosing to obey God, even if we're facing difficult times, especially if we're facing difficult times.

34
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:25,860
And so, I'm looking forward to this challenge for us to be obedient in the midst of whatever circumstances we might face moving forward.

35
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:33,480
So, what I want to do is I want to read the first verse of James, kind of give us some context for the book, maybe like a preface to the sermon series.

36
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:41,060
And then I'll pray, and then we're going to hop into the book of James and see how far we get, which, again, as a planner, I don't like this.

37
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:44,800
I've got a couple of alternate endings written in my notes, because I don't know how far we're going to get.

38
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:48,740
But, I think it'll be good.

39
00:03:48,740 --> 00:03:49,820
Does that sound good?

40
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:50,880
All right.

41
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:54,340
So, James chapter 1, verse 1, says this.

42
00:03:54,340 --> 00:03:59,780
This letter is from James, a slave of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ.

43
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:06,320
I am writing to the 12 tribes, Jewish believers scattered abroad, greetings.

44
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:12,040
So, this is important from the outset to realize who our author is and who he's writing to.

45
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:14,940
James is the half-brother of Jesus.

46
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:17,600
So, talk about apologetics, right?

47
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:31,460
Like, if you're in here and you've ever questioned or doubted whether or not the claims of Jesus are true or not, just think for me, with me for a second, that the brother of Jesus is calling Jesus his Lord.

48
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:37,200
He's saying, I am a slave to the divinity of my brother.

49
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:38,780
Any of you have brothers in the room?

50
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:41,240
Like, that's a crazy concept to think about.

51
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:51,020
A crazy concept to think that, ultimately, Josephus tells us that James is going to be martyred for the fact that he is claiming that Jesus is God.

52
00:04:51,440 --> 00:05:00,920
So, his brother is saying, I'm willing to give my life for the claim, for the truth, that my brother is the Son of God.

53
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:03,280
He is who he says he is.

54
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:07,960
He laid down his life as a ransom for many.

55
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:11,340
So, James, the brother of Jesus, is writing this letter.

56
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:16,640
And James was an influential church leader in the church of Jerusalem.

57
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:20,780
So, James was an influential church leader in the church of Jerusalem.

58
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:26,800
Mainly Jewish converts is his specific area of leadership.

59
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:33,660
And what happened, we see in the book of Acts, is that the church in Jerusalem was scattered because of persecution.

60
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:42,260
And so, James had this really powerful, influential congregation in a really religious city and an important city.

61
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:45,900
And because of persecution, all of these believers are scattered all over the place.

62
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:55,040
And so, James is writing this letter to these people who have been scattered to encourage them to continue to obey the message of Jesus.

63
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,580
It's a very practical book.

64
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:59,580
It's actually going to mirror, in a lot of ways, the Sermon on the Mount.

65
00:05:59,580 --> 00:06:08,960
It's like James, as the brother of Jesus, kind of reiterating one of the most important teachings that his brother ever gave in the Sermon on the Mount.

66
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:15,340
So, imagine with me a group of people who are in an amazing community, like-minded people,

67
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:19,260
in a location rich with opportunity for worship and discipleship.

68
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:21,640
That's the Jewish believers in Jerusalem, right?

69
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:22,860
Like, they had it all going for them.

70
00:06:22,860 --> 00:06:25,760
Jerusalem was like the hub of Judaism.

71
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,420
So, they're in Jerusalem.

72
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:31,400
They're following Jesus together with people who understand the Scriptures.

73
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:38,860
And then overnight, they're uprooted, isolated, and confused about the future.

74
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:44,960
I don't know about you, but man, can I relate to that backdrop?

75
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:51,740
Can I relate to a group of people who have been uprooted, isolated, and who are confused about their future?

76
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:53,100
I'm sure many of us can relate.

77
00:06:53,100 --> 00:07:00,820
And James writes this book to encourage them to continue to obey Jesus, no matter how much their experience might change.

78
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:06,100
And James isn't going to talk a lot about theology throughout this book.

79
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:09,540
Like, a lot of Paul's books, right, he's working through theology.

80
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:13,440
He's trying to teach people about their faith and what their faith looks like.

81
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:21,980
But he's pretty confident that these people understand the message of Jesus, but he wants to make sure that they obey the message of Jesus.

82
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:34,480
And so, the reason I feel so led to this book is pastorally, I think it's a great book for us to dive into because a lot of us can relate to that idea of feeling uprooted or isolated or confused about the future.

83
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:39,820
I think that 2020, 2021, 2022, all of us have felt these feelings before.

84
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:51,620
And also, like, the church in America, I used to say this a lot in my previous church, like, I feel like the church in America is often educated beyond our obedience, right?

85
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:57,920
Like, we, it's not like we need a lot of theology lessons because, like, we're sort of, like, you probably have three or four Bible apps on your phone.

86
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:02,140
Like, there's teachings all over the Internet of the Bible.

87
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:03,380
There's so much theology.

88
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:11,080
We have so much, like, backdrop of theology in our culture, but so often, like, we don't obey it.

89
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:11,780
We know it.

90
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:15,000
Our head is filled with knowledge that our lives don't live out.

91
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,860
Like, we were talking about this in my small group this week.

92
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:22,700
Like, there's underground churches in China that have, like, one or two pages of Scripture that they share together.

93
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:28,120
And yet, in the midst of persecution, they're giving their lives for their faith.

94
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:30,600
And we have three or four Bible apps on our phone.

95
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:32,140
And it's not a bad thing.

96
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:32,860
Like, that's a good thing.

97
00:08:32,860 --> 00:08:35,840
I'm not, like, laying heavy guilt on us.

98
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:37,980
But what I'm saying is we have the information.

99
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:42,220
But how often do we live that information out?

100
00:08:42,220 --> 00:08:51,200
And so, my prayer, as we work through the book of James, is that we would be encouraged to have hope, no matter what our circumstances might lead us into,

101
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:58,500
ultimately, that we would be willing to obey the practical teachings of Jesus, even when they're hard.

102
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:07,320
Like, the book of James is going to tell us, like, not to consider wealthy people higher than poor people.

103
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:10,700
Like, he's going to say, lay down your lives to serve those who struggle.

104
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:19,240
He's going to give us hard commands about not being angry, about not gossiping about one another, about literally, like, hard things.

105
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:24,540
And so, my prayer for us in this series is that we would just become more like Jesus.

106
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:33,520
Like, as a community of believers, we would become more like Jesus, that our heads wouldn't be filled with information, that our feet and hands don't walk out.

107
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:36,020
Does that sound like a good plan?

108
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:37,820
All right, go ahead.

109
00:09:37,820 --> 00:09:41,000
So, let me pray, and then we'll see how far we get.

110
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:46,460
I'm hoping for, like, 12 verses, but it might be three or four.

111
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:47,240
We'll see.

112
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:59,720
Father, we thank you so much for this day and this opportunity that we have to gather together under your word, influenced by your Holy Spirit.

113
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:12,360
Holy Spirit, I pray that you would be present and active in this room, encouraging us, pointing us to truth, challenging us with our perspective on trials, and teaching us to obey your word.

114
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:17,880
So, I see that people who truly believe that following you is better than anything else.

115
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:20,520
You are better than anything else.

116
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:24,360
May our lives reflect that, not just our songs, but our lives.

117
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:27,440
So, in Jesus' name I pray, amen.

118
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:36,840
So, I don't know about any of you, but I am a master at doing dumb things that negatively impact my life.

119
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:43,840
Anybody else in the room, like, feel like you regularly do stupid stuff and it negatively impacts your life?

120
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,220
All right, we got a lot of humble people in the room.

121
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:48,860
I'm so thankful that you guys are with me.

122
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:55,740
I was afraid when I, like, went through my notes by myself, I imagined that all of you were like, no, that's just you, bro.

123
00:10:55,740 --> 00:11:02,320
Hey, man, a couple weeks ago, or maybe a couple months ago at this point, I had an errand day.

124
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:07,860
And I like to jam-pack my errand days, like, just get as much stuff as I can possibly get done done.

125
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:12,400
And, like, I'm a box checker, and so I had this list of things that I wanted to do.

126
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:16,520
And I was just, like, trying to get through as many things as I could possibly do.

127
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:19,700
And so I was at this, I was in this parking lot at Books a Million.

128
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:22,060
Is that me?

129
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:22,580
That's not me.

130
00:11:22,580 --> 00:11:22,940
Okay.

131
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:24,900
You guys are done with me already.

132
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:26,740
I was at this parking lot at Books a Million.

133
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:28,620
My wife's laughing because she knows exactly what happened.

134
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:30,360
And I was in between two errands.

135
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:32,340
I was going, like, three miles an hour in the parking lot.

136
00:11:32,340 --> 00:11:35,120
And I was, like, at the back of the parking lot, totally empty.

137
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,100
I looked around.

138
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,920
I was like, I can check some e-mails right now.

139
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:44,340
I'll be super productive by checking e-mails in between errands while I'm operating a motor vehicle.

140
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:45,080
I know.

141
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:47,460
We should not be doing these things.

142
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:49,180
This is unwise and foolish.

143
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:51,420
But I thought I would be productive.

144
00:11:51,420 --> 00:11:57,940
I opened up my phone, checked a couple of e-mails, and there's this part in the parking lot.

145
00:11:57,940 --> 00:12:01,220
It's kind of like the Kohl's parking lot turns into the Books a Million parking lot.

146
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:08,200
And a little, like, a little, you know, concrete slab comes further out than it was in the Kohl's parking lot.

147
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:12,700
And I hit it going about four miles an hour and slashed my tire wide open.

148
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:18,580
And also, awesome, there was a guy chilling in the bag of the parking lot watching the whole thing.

149
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:20,120
So that's even more embarrassing.

150
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:21,700
Right?

151
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:25,300
But it was like, from that moment on, the rest of my errands were ruined.

152
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:27,360
Like, I had to call the insurance company.

153
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,320
I had to get the car.

154
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:30,120
They had to come, fix the tire.

155
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:34,900
And then I had to take the car to the shop because, you know, the new tire is not a real tire.

156
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:39,880
It was like, my whole day was gone because I made a foolish decision.

157
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,960
But here's the thing.

158
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,880
Like, in situations like this, they stink, right?

159
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:47,380
There's negative consequences to our bad decisions.

160
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:53,440
But we can either choose to learn valuable lessons from situations like this,

161
00:12:53,440 --> 00:13:01,000
or we can waste an opportunity to learn a valuable lesson by doing the same thing again and again and again.

162
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:07,340
And you would think, it's only been a couple months from now, you would think that I would have learned a lesson to put my phone somewhere where I can't reach it.

163
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:11,340
But sometimes I want to change my podcast still, right?

164
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:14,680
And like, one of these days, I'm going to have to learn this lesson all over again.

165
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:22,140
And if I don't choose to learn a lesson from my mistakes, then oftentimes I might waste an opportunity.

166
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:29,640
As we hop into these next couple verses in James, in our passage this morning, James is going to make it very clear for followers of Jesus.

167
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:37,380
If you're a follower of Jesus, that there is a specific goal for every trial you face, every difficult situation that you go through.

168
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:38,900
Like, there's a purpose behind it.

169
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:39,880
You can learn from it.

170
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:42,600
You can grow through it if you choose to.

171
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:50,120
Whether it be a trial that you bring on your own by making a foolish decision or a trial that is brought on by other people around you.

172
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:54,820
There is a specific goal that God has for every one of your trials.

173
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:58,520
If I were to summarize the next couple of verses, I would say it this way.

174
00:13:58,520 --> 00:14:04,400
That the positive outcome of various trials is spiritual maturity.

175
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:08,740
If you get anything else from my message this morning, I want you to hear this.

176
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:14,660
For followers of Jesus, there should be, there can be a positive outcome from all of your trials.

177
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:19,000
And that positive outcome should be spiritual maturity.

178
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:22,340
It says this in James 1, verse 2.

179
00:14:22,420 --> 00:14:39,400
When trials come, when troubles come, when difficulty comes, consider it an opportunity for great joy.

180
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:39,860
Why?

181
00:14:39,860 --> 00:14:41,860
Why would we have joy in trials?

182
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:42,920
We have joy in trials.

183
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:43,180
Why?

184
00:14:43,180 --> 00:14:49,580
For you know that when your faith is tested, your endurance has a chance to grow.

185
00:14:49,580 --> 00:14:51,440
It doesn't say it automatically grows.

186
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:54,340
Your endurance has a chance, an opportunity to grow.

187
00:14:54,340 --> 00:14:57,280
So you choose, decide, let it grow.

188
00:14:57,280 --> 00:15:04,620
For when your endurance is fully developed, you will be perfect and complete, needing nothing.

189
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:11,380
James is going to tell believers, like, when trials come, when difficulty comes, choose a joyful perspective.

190
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:13,200
Choose to view your trials with joy.

191
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:13,420
Why?

192
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:15,660
Because a positive outcome can come out of them.

193
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:19,000
Like, trials can conform you to the image of Jesus.

194
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,840
Trials can bring about spiritual maturity.

195
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:27,360
The positive outcome of various trials is spiritual maturity.

196
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:31,180
So let's unpack that statement a little bit.

197
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:33,320
The positive outcome.

198
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:39,700
He says, when troubles of any kind come your way, choose joy.

199
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:45,960
As I was thinking about this, this is a pretty well-known passage that Christians like to put on coffee mugs.

200
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:47,480
We talk about that a lot at Canvas Church.

201
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:48,720
Coffee mug verses, right?

202
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:50,420
Consider it all joy.

203
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:59,120
And if we're just being honest, most likely our natural response, our first response to trial, to difficulty, is not joy.

204
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:03,240
I didn't hit that curb and think, I'm going to learn a lesson.

205
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:08,000
I am never going to pick up my phone in the car again.

206
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,940
No, I thought, man, this is terrible.

207
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:11,160
My day is ruined.

208
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:18,540
I wasted probably all of our excess spending for the month's budget because of a stupid decision that I made.

209
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:28,400
Nothing makes me more joyful than to go to my wife and tell her that we can't go to a restaurant this week because I have to fix my tire that I popped because I was on my phone in the parking lot.

210
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:29,720
That was not a fun conversation.

211
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:34,200
Most likely, it's not our natural response to say, awesome.

212
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,680
My marriage is in turmoil.

213
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:43,420
I'm on the brink, and it's on the brink of ending, but I can't wait to see how God is going to use this for good in my life.

214
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:45,340
Sweet.

215
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:54,140
I don't have enough money in my bank account to pay both of these bills, but I sure am excited to see how God is going to use this to make me more like Jesus.

216
00:16:55,240 --> 00:17:00,860
My child is making bad decisions and going in a direction that I wouldn't have chose for their life.

217
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:04,160
This diagnosis from the doctor was worse than I expected.

218
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:05,860
My best friend betrayed me.

219
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:08,060
This is going to be a great opportunity.

220
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:11,560
No, like that's real talk here.

221
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:13,660
Like that's not our natural reaction.

222
00:17:13,660 --> 00:17:19,520
And I think for so many Christians, we put this undue pressure on ourselves.

223
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:21,060
We misinterpret this text.

224
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:25,660
And we say we have to have joy in the midst of circumstances.

225
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:26,560
It has to be natural.

226
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:28,000
It just has to come out of us.

227
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:33,980
So I want to this morning really quickly talk to my over-spiritual people and my skeptics.

228
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:38,140
Like over-spiritual people, James isn't saying that it should be natural.

229
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,220
It should just come out of you.

230
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:40,920
Like, oh, yay, trials are here.

231
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:42,140
I'm so happy.

232
00:17:42,140 --> 00:17:44,180
That's insane.

233
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:50,460
But far too many Christians, we become hypocrites because we misread this text,

234
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:54,760
and we think we have to just be excited every time a trial comes our way.

235
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:56,920
So we pretend that it's our natural reaction.

236
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:58,580
Like we put on a fake face.

237
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:00,040
We're like, God's going to be mad at us.

238
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:02,620
God's going to be mad at me if I don't have joy in this circumstance.

239
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:04,100
So man, am I joyful.

240
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:10,980
And then to the skeptics in the room, like how many of you have almost walked away from the church altogether

241
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:15,720
because people like this who are fake and pretend like everything's great when nothing is great.

242
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:21,680
James isn't saying it's a natural reaction.

243
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:26,280
He's saying, look at the language.

244
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:29,520
He says consider it an opportunity for great joy.

245
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:31,200
Like pre-decide.

246
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:39,100
Like when trials come your way, you can choose to have joy even when your feelings don't reflect that.

247
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:43,160
Because oftentimes, like our feelings follow our faith.

248
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:49,160
Oftentimes we have to believe that God is good in the midst of a difficult circumstance,

249
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:51,860
even when our feelings are saying, this is not fun.

250
00:18:51,860 --> 00:18:54,100
But we pre-decide.

251
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:54,980
We make a decision.

252
00:18:54,980 --> 00:18:56,080
Why do we make a decision?

253
00:18:56,080 --> 00:18:57,980
Because there can be a positive outcome.

254
00:18:57,980 --> 00:19:03,800
We know that trials can make us more like Jesus until we pre-decide.

255
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:09,160
Like we use this line all the time in our church, real people with real lives.

256
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:14,820
Like in this church, real people with real lives would tell you trials really suck for us too.

257
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:17,740
Like we don't just have this natural, joyful reaction.

258
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:21,040
And James isn't saying our natural reaction to suffering should be joy.

259
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:25,340
He's saying if we want to walk out of our trials with a positive outcome.

260
00:19:25,340 --> 00:19:33,120
Like if we don't want to waste our trial, then we choose, we pre-decide to have joy in the midst of our trial

261
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:35,840
because we know it can make us more like Jesus.

262
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:38,700
I think about Jesus, who's our perfect example.

263
00:19:38,700 --> 00:19:42,520
Right before he was about to go to the cross, he's in the Garden of Gethsemane,

264
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:48,220
and he's praying, and he's sweating drops of blood because he doesn't want to go to the cross.

265
00:19:48,220 --> 00:19:52,720
His emotional reaction isn't, oh yay, I can't wait to go to the cross.

266
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:56,020
But ultimately, he pre-decides.

267
00:19:56,020 --> 00:19:59,260
Hebrews says, for the joy set before him.

268
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:05,580
He pre-decides that he's going to go through the cross because he knows the positive outcome on the other side.

269
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:07,460
And that's our example.

270
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:08,760
We pre-decide.

271
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:13,640
When trials come our way, we choose to receive a positive outcome from it.

272
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:19,460
We choose to view this trial as an opportunity for us to become more like Jesus.

273
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:25,540
The best illustration I could come up with is, when I went to college, you know,

274
00:20:25,540 --> 00:20:31,600
you're supposed to go to college, like, with the intent of learning how to do the thing that you want to do for the rest of your life.

275
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:38,860
I wish I could go back to college and pre-decide to view my classes in a much more responsible way.

276
00:20:38,860 --> 00:20:45,600
I went to college, like, to have fun and to build relationships and, like, to get a diploma.

277
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:48,460
Which means, I didn't go to my class to learn.

278
00:20:48,460 --> 00:20:50,760
I went to my class to get my assignments.

279
00:20:50,760 --> 00:20:52,900
I did my assignments to get a grade.

280
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:56,780
Usually a C plus, B minus was what I was going for.

281
00:20:56,780 --> 00:21:05,300
But, like, how many hours of classes did I waste because I was just there to check a box?

282
00:21:05,300 --> 00:21:07,300
I was just there to get through it.

283
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:12,920
And oftentimes, I think about some of the classes I have and how they relate to some of the experiences I've gone through.

284
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:16,080
And I'm like, man, I really should have paid more attention in that class.

285
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:23,960
I really should have pre-decided in those moments that I wanted the outcome of that class to be, I'm going to learn through this.

286
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:27,100
And that's what James is saying about trials.

287
00:21:27,100 --> 00:21:31,480
Like, we enter trials with this mindset of, I'm going to learn something through this.

288
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:33,060
I don't want to be in this situation.

289
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:34,500
I'd rather not have this trial.

290
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:38,100
But since I can't get out of it, I'm going to have a positive outcome through it.

291
00:21:38,100 --> 00:21:41,360
I'm going to be conformed to the image of Jesus.

292
00:21:41,360 --> 00:21:43,540
And that's the goal of every believer, right?

293
00:21:43,540 --> 00:21:50,180
Like, Romans 8, 29 says, for those whom he foreknew, he also predestined to be conformed to the image of Jesus.

294
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:56,240
That verse tells us that literally the purpose of followers of Jesus is to become more like Jesus.

295
00:21:56,240 --> 00:22:01,820
And trials, difficulty, is a cheat code for spiritual maturity.

296
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:08,740
We say that again, trials, difficult seasons in our life, they are a cheat code for spiritual maturity.

297
00:22:08,740 --> 00:22:15,220
Like, it happens, we're conformed to the image of Jesus faster through trials than we are through good times.

298
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:19,500
Later in this passage, like, James is going to talk about rich people and poor people.

299
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:24,840
And he's going to say, like, poor people are blessed because they are just naturally more dependent on God.

300
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:28,320
Like, they have to wake up every moment and be dependent on God.

301
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:33,580
Like, spiritual maturity happens faster when there's difficulty, when there's trial.

302
00:22:33,580 --> 00:22:38,940
Our small group, we just started talking about spiritual habits and practices.

303
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:46,100
And so, like, yeah, Bible study, fellowship and prayer, service, community, Sabbath and confession, accountability.

304
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:53,180
Like, all of these things, if we build them into our life, can help conform us into the image of Jesus, can help make us more like Jesus.

305
00:22:53,180 --> 00:22:57,640
But it's slow over time, like, it accumulates very slowly.

306
00:22:57,640 --> 00:23:07,280
But when you put us in the pressure cooker of life, trials, difficult situations, those things make us conform to the image of Jesus faster than anything else.

307
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:11,920
Best way I can illustrate it is, how many of you guys have been to a Kiwi football game recently?

308
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:14,780
Anybody seen, like, little kids play football?

309
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:15,420
A couple of you.

310
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:20,080
Well, just imagine with me, like, when little kids play football, they move very slowly.

311
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:24,960
Because they weigh, like, 40 pounds, and then, like, they have, like, 20 pounds on their back.

312
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:29,080
So imagine trying to run as fast as you can with half of your body weight on you.

313
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:30,560
Like, it doesn't happen.

314
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:35,580
And so, like, you watch them, and they're, like, moving, like, literally in slow motion.

315
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:36,800
And they, like, touch each other.

316
00:23:37,160 --> 00:23:40,340
And they both, like, fall over very slowly, right?

317
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:43,200
But, like, next week's the Super Bowl.

318
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:51,340
Think about, think about how impressive athletes moving at, like, 4-2-40, 4-3-40 speeds, full speed ahead.

319
00:23:51,340 --> 00:23:53,420
Like, think about how quickly those things happen.

320
00:23:53,420 --> 00:23:57,600
But here's what I felt the Lord giving me this morning with this illustration.

321
00:23:57,600 --> 00:24:06,220
It's, like, when you're moving slower, like, when everything's normal and fine and good, like, when bad things happen, it doesn't have that much of an impact.

322
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:15,320
But at full speed, professional athletes, when they hit head-to-head, like, the trauma can be overwhelming.

323
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:25,960
And so, like, when things are difficult, when, like, our life is just overwhelmed, like, those things, we can be conformed to the image of Jesus faster and better than any other situation.

324
00:24:25,960 --> 00:24:31,040
But on the flip side, nothing can derail our faith faster than a trial.

325
00:24:32,220 --> 00:24:40,960
I see so many people walk away from their faith because of the situation, a circumstance in their life that they blame on God, like, so often.

326
00:24:40,960 --> 00:24:51,180
Just as quickly as trials can conform us to the image of Jesus faster than regular good life can, trials can make us walk away from God faster.

327
00:24:51,180 --> 00:24:55,240
I think about the story of a guy named Job in the Bible.

328
00:24:55,360 --> 00:24:57,040
A lot of you are probably familiar with Job, right?

329
00:24:57,040 --> 00:25:05,260
Like, Job was wealthy and blessed, and Satan asked God if he could test Job, and overnight, Job lost everything.

330
00:25:05,260 --> 00:25:06,300
Everything.

331
00:25:06,300 --> 00:25:13,340
And through that trial, him and his wife both chose two very different responses.

332
00:25:14,940 --> 00:25:19,820
Job's wife looked at Job, and she said, curse, we should just curse God and die.

333
00:25:19,820 --> 00:25:22,980
Like, this trial, this, it's overwhelming.

334
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:28,300
We can't, like, we can't continue to have faith in a God that would allow this to happen.

335
00:25:28,300 --> 00:25:32,620
And Job says, naked I came from my mother's womb, and naked shall I return.

336
00:25:32,620 --> 00:25:34,200
Blessed be the name of the Lord.

337
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:40,000
And so often, I think, Christians, we view trial as just neutral.

338
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:41,580
Like, we just want to get through it.

339
00:25:43,580 --> 00:25:47,180
And personally and pastorally, I think trials are going to do one of two things.

340
00:25:47,180 --> 00:25:51,480
They're either going to push you away from God and de-form you from the image of Jesus,

341
00:25:51,480 --> 00:25:52,620
or they're going to draw you closer.

342
00:25:52,620 --> 00:25:55,660
And what matters is what we decide to do in those moments.

343
00:25:55,660 --> 00:25:57,500
And James here is saying, you can have joy.

344
00:25:57,500 --> 00:26:06,340
You can pre-decide to have joy in the midst of trials because you know a positive outcome can come out of this.

345
00:26:06,340 --> 00:26:09,420
So many Christians, we just want to push through trials.

346
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:12,320
But we shouldn't rush through trials.

347
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:18,960
We should pre-decide to have joy in the midst of trials because we know that they can produce a positive outcome.

348
00:26:21,100 --> 00:26:25,800
Positive outcome of various trials is spiritual maturity.

349
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:29,320
So, moving on, right?

350
00:26:29,320 --> 00:26:30,620
Various trials.

351
00:26:30,620 --> 00:26:39,080
It might be really tempting for us to say, yeah, Ryan, like, that's all well and good, but this is Scripture.

352
00:26:39,080 --> 00:26:39,860
It's spiritual.

353
00:26:40,240 --> 00:26:43,820
And so, James must be talking about a really specific type of trial.

354
00:26:43,820 --> 00:26:48,160
Like, he must be talking about one of those Job situations where, like, God is in the midst of it.

355
00:26:48,160 --> 00:26:49,140
God is ordaining it.

356
00:26:49,140 --> 00:26:53,240
Like, there's only certain trials in which we should have joy.

357
00:26:53,240 --> 00:26:56,800
Like, everyday life, when you run over the curb, that doesn't count.

358
00:26:56,800 --> 00:26:57,920
Like, that's not spiritual.

359
00:26:57,920 --> 00:26:59,480
That's just you being foolish.

360
00:26:59,480 --> 00:27:00,800
No, James gets ahead of this.

361
00:27:01,340 --> 00:27:14,320
He says, when various different kinds of troubles come your way, he knows that he's talking to a very diverse group of believers who have been scattered to all different kinds of areas and situations.

362
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:17,940
And he's saying it doesn't matter what type of trial comes your way.

363
00:27:17,940 --> 00:27:22,740
Any type of trial can be used by God to conform you to the image of Jesus.

364
00:27:22,880 --> 00:27:27,880
So when any type of trial enters your life, you can choose joy in the midst of it.

365
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:31,220
I'm just trying to think of the types of trials that we face.

366
00:27:31,220 --> 00:27:32,120
I came up with four.

367
00:27:32,120 --> 00:27:34,240
I'm sure there's probably more.

368
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:38,720
But the first type of trial I thought of is one that's brought on by yourself.

369
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:39,460
Right?

370
00:27:39,460 --> 00:27:40,460
Like, you sin.

371
00:27:40,460 --> 00:27:42,500
You make an unwise decision.

372
00:27:42,500 --> 00:27:43,720
You're lazy.

373
00:27:43,720 --> 00:27:49,700
You make some decisions that ultimately lead to a trial or a difficulty in your life.

374
00:27:49,700 --> 00:27:51,540
Me hitting the curb was my fault.

375
00:27:51,540 --> 00:27:52,560
A difficult situation.

376
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:55,080
That I brought upon myself.

377
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:59,540
And oftentimes, rather than joy, when we make bad decisions, what are the natural reactions?

378
00:27:59,540 --> 00:28:01,900
The natural reaction is guilt and shame.

379
00:28:01,900 --> 00:28:03,560
I did this.

380
00:28:03,560 --> 00:28:04,620
I deserve this.

381
00:28:04,620 --> 00:28:06,300
I am guilty.

382
00:28:06,300 --> 00:28:08,320
I don't deserve God's grace.

383
00:28:08,320 --> 00:28:10,120
I can't have joy in this situation.

384
00:28:10,120 --> 00:28:11,340
I got myself here.

385
00:28:11,340 --> 00:28:15,700
I've got to pick myself up by my bootstraps and fix this situation.

386
00:28:15,700 --> 00:28:21,400
James is saying, listen, if trials have come your way because you made bad decisions,

387
00:28:21,620 --> 00:28:28,240
and your natural reaction is guilt and shame, don't allow those things to control you through this trial.

388
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:30,660
You can choose joy.

389
00:28:30,660 --> 00:28:32,760
You can receive the grace and forgiveness of God.

390
00:28:32,820 --> 00:28:33,840
You can't go back in time and change the situation.

391
00:28:33,840 --> 00:28:34,960
You can't go back in time and change the situation.

392
00:28:34,960 --> 00:28:37,980
But you can respond now moving forward.

393
00:28:37,980 --> 00:28:40,020
I think about King David.

394
00:28:40,020 --> 00:28:48,360
King David had an affair and then murdered the husband of the woman that he had an affair with.

395
00:28:49,860 --> 00:28:58,120
And the rest of his life moving forward had to have been crippled with guilt and shame and the negative consequences of the decisions that he made.

396
00:28:58,640 --> 00:29:03,660
And then ultimately, God, in his grace, sent a prophet to confront David, a prophet named Nathan.

397
00:29:03,660 --> 00:29:07,700
And he said, David, like, your life is miserable.

398
00:29:07,700 --> 00:29:11,660
You've made these decisions that are so negative and so terrible.

399
00:29:11,660 --> 00:29:17,100
And it's in that moment where David chooses to repent, to ask for forgiveness.

400
00:29:17,220 --> 00:29:18,980
And he says this in Psalm chapter 51.

401
00:29:18,980 --> 00:29:24,740
He says, God, restore to me the joy of my salvation.

402
00:29:24,740 --> 00:29:28,460
So I don't know where you're at in the room.

403
00:29:28,460 --> 00:29:33,280
If you're in here and you've made some really unwise decisions that have led to some really difficult situations in your life,

404
00:29:33,280 --> 00:29:39,840
and maybe you're crippled with the shame and the guilt wishing you could go back in time and change the decisions that you made that got you here.

405
00:29:41,220 --> 00:29:47,260
Man, I'm here this morning to tell you, like, you can't go back in time, but you can choose how you respond from now moving forward.

406
00:29:47,260 --> 00:29:52,500
You can bring that sin, that guilt, that shame to God and ask for forgiveness.

407
00:29:52,500 --> 00:29:55,040
And pray the same prayer that David prayed.

408
00:29:55,040 --> 00:29:58,020
God, restore to me joy in my salvation.

409
00:29:58,020 --> 00:30:05,920
Let me see this trial as positive moving forward because I know that you can use it to conform me into the image of Jesus.

410
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:10,640
So trials you bring on yourself, trials that are brought on by other people.

411
00:30:10,640 --> 00:30:16,200
Well, how often do other people's sin negatively affect us during about difficult situations in our life?

412
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:20,320
And oftentimes our response then is anger and bitterness, right?

413
00:30:20,320 --> 00:30:21,920
Like we want justice.

414
00:30:21,920 --> 00:30:24,240
How dare they do that to us?

415
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:27,340
How dare they lead us into a situation like this?

416
00:30:27,340 --> 00:30:33,680
And rather than viewing that trial that somebody else brought on us with joy and say, God's going to use this for a positive outcome.

417
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:37,480
I'm not happy that I'm here, but God can use this.

418
00:30:37,480 --> 00:30:40,280
This is exactly what Jesus went through.

419
00:30:41,600 --> 00:30:41,720
Right?

420
00:30:41,720 --> 00:30:46,480
Like his trials, his suffering was brought about by no decisions of his own.

421
00:30:46,480 --> 00:30:47,560
Jesus was sinless.

422
00:30:47,560 --> 00:30:52,220
And the decisions of other people led him to trial and difficulty.

423
00:30:52,220 --> 00:30:53,400
And what did he say on the cross?

424
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:56,940
He said, forgive them, for they know not what they do.

425
00:30:58,740 --> 00:31:02,760
When trials are brought on to you by other people, we follow the example of Jesus.

426
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:05,380
We choose to get a positive outcome.

427
00:31:05,380 --> 00:31:06,300
We don't want to be there.

428
00:31:06,300 --> 00:31:13,080
And forgiveness, again, forgiveness doesn't always mean that you put yourself back in the same situation to get hurt again.

429
00:31:14,080 --> 00:31:18,760
But you choose to extend the forgiveness that Jesus forgave those who sinned against him.

430
00:31:18,760 --> 00:31:23,920
And you find joy because you know you can be conformed to the image of Jesus through that trial.

431
00:31:23,920 --> 00:31:28,980
Another type of trial is just the effects of living in a fallen, broken world.

432
00:31:30,260 --> 00:31:38,400
Sickness, poverty, all kinds of things happen just because, like, sin has entered the world and have broken God's original design.

433
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:42,220
So often this leads us to depression and overwhelming anxiety.

434
00:31:42,640 --> 00:31:46,920
Because no matter how hard we work to get ahead, we can't.

435
00:31:46,920 --> 00:31:51,620
No matter how many hours we put in, the bank account's still empty.

436
00:31:51,620 --> 00:31:57,660
No matter how many vitamins and supplements and exercise we do, we still get a bad diagnosis.

437
00:31:57,660 --> 00:32:04,720
There's effects of living in a fallen world.

438
00:32:04,720 --> 00:32:09,300
In John 9, they went by this guy who was blind.

439
00:32:09,980 --> 00:32:14,540
And the disciples asked Jesus, like, is he blind because he sinned or because his parents sinned?

440
00:32:14,540 --> 00:32:17,020
Jesus is like, no, it's not about sin.

441
00:32:17,020 --> 00:32:23,260
Like, we live in a fallen world and God can get glory through it.

442
00:32:23,260 --> 00:32:30,420
So if you're just, like, broken down by the effects of a sinful, fallen world, like, take that to God.

443
00:32:30,420 --> 00:32:33,400
And ask that he give you joy in the midst of it.

444
00:32:33,400 --> 00:32:39,000
Lastly, that supernatural type of trial like Job went through.

445
00:32:39,980 --> 00:32:47,080
Oftentimes, God can use those to work in some incredible ways.

446
00:32:47,080 --> 00:32:51,860
So the reasons for your trial shouldn't affect your overall approach to the trial.

447
00:32:51,860 --> 00:32:56,320
Whether it's your fault, somebody else's fault, or really nobody's fault.

448
00:32:56,320 --> 00:33:03,020
We pre-decide that we're going to allow the trial to conform us into the image of Jesus.

449
00:33:03,220 --> 00:33:07,040
Each type of various trial can lead us to spiritual maturity.

450
00:33:07,040 --> 00:33:12,960
No matter the source of your trials, there are all opportunities for you to be conformed to the image of Jesus.

451
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:17,300
If you brought it on yourself, repent and receive the grace of God and move forward.

452
00:33:17,840 --> 00:33:24,240
If it was brought on by somebody else, learn to forgive them, following the example of Jesus, and move forward.

453
00:33:24,240 --> 00:33:33,700
If it's due to a fallen world or a spiritual trial, pray to God for healing and deliverance and seek to find contentment in the midst of your circumstances.

454
00:33:34,920 --> 00:33:37,840
And remember, we have a great high priest.

455
00:33:37,840 --> 00:33:43,500
Hebrews says that Jesus suffered in every way that we did, and yet he chose not to sin.

456
00:33:43,500 --> 00:33:46,620
He chose joy through the midst of trials.

457
00:33:46,620 --> 00:33:51,380
The positive outcome of various trials is spiritual maturity.

458
00:33:51,380 --> 00:33:54,760
What does spiritual maturity look like?

459
00:33:56,040 --> 00:34:02,600
This word is translated as perfect, but for my study, it's actually better rendered mature.

460
00:34:02,600 --> 00:34:04,360
So let it grow.

461
00:34:04,360 --> 00:34:10,900
Let your endurance grow, and when it is fully developed, you will be mature and complete, lacking nothing.

462
00:34:10,900 --> 00:34:15,320
Spiritual maturity is ultimately about becoming more like Jesus.

463
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:20,920
In our small group this week, we talked about, you guys remember the WWJD bracelets?

464
00:34:20,920 --> 00:34:21,940
It's a big thing.

465
00:34:21,940 --> 00:34:23,060
What would Jesus do?

466
00:34:24,040 --> 00:34:35,920
And this author that I've been listening to a lot recently, he said, if I could redo that, if I could change that thing, he said it's not very marketable, because it would be WWJD IHWM.

467
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:40,940
It doesn't look good on a bracelet, but what would Jesus do if he were me?

468
00:34:40,940 --> 00:34:52,140
Like, so often we over-spiritualize situations, and, like, we need to just ask ourselves, like, in this moment, in this trial, what would Jesus do if he were me?

469
00:34:52,840 --> 00:35:01,600
We talked about this in our small group, and one of the dads said, like, man, so often I read Scripture, I see Jesus doing these incredible things, and I ask myself, what would Jesus do?

470
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:05,180
I think, should I, like, go, like, on to a mountain and just start preaching?

471
00:35:05,180 --> 00:35:11,240
And he goes, no, like, Jesus, if he were a dad, he wouldn't just abandon his children and go preach on a mountain.

472
00:35:11,240 --> 00:35:12,960
Like, he would be a good dad.

473
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:14,380
He would be a good husband.

474
00:35:14,380 --> 00:35:17,460
He would go through these trials in specific ways.

475
00:35:17,460 --> 00:35:22,360
And so spiritual maturity for us looks like, what would Jesus do if he were me?

476
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:26,360
And what's the end goal?

477
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:33,340
The end goal is spiritual maturity, which leaves you complete and lacking nothing.

478
00:35:35,080 --> 00:35:47,040
Why would it be important for a group of believers who are interdependent in relationship with one another, why would it be important for us to get to a point where we're mature and we need nothing?

479
00:35:49,740 --> 00:35:52,480
So we can help others alongside of us, right?

480
00:35:52,480 --> 00:36:05,080
Like, if all of us are always crippled under the weight of our trials, we never learn, we never grow, we never learn the lessons that the trials bring about, then we can no longer come alongside somebody else and help them through their trials.

481
00:36:05,080 --> 00:36:09,760
And so James is saying that in spiritual maturity, it's so important how we view our trials.

482
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:22,540
It's so important that we get through our trials learning lessons, growing in spiritual maturity, because then we can come alongside other brothers and sisters who are going through similar trials that we're going through, and we can give them hope.

483
00:36:22,540 --> 00:36:29,280
We can preach to them that there's hope on the other side of this suffering.

484
00:36:29,280 --> 00:36:31,380
I think about Moses.

485
00:36:31,380 --> 00:36:42,480
There's this battle that the Israelites are in, and God says, Moses, as long as you have your staff raised above your head, the Israelite army will continue to win this battle.

486
00:36:42,480 --> 00:36:46,100
And so Moses is up on this mountain with his staff over his head.

487
00:36:46,100 --> 00:36:48,120
He's tired.

488
00:36:48,120 --> 00:36:52,100
And the staff starts to drop, and the army starts to lose.

489
00:36:52,100 --> 00:36:55,720
And he muscles up more strength and energy, and he gets it up.

490
00:36:55,720 --> 00:36:59,820
And eventually his brother Aaron comes alongside him and helps him hold up his staff.

491
00:36:59,820 --> 00:37:03,980
And I think it's such a great illustration for those of us who are going through trials.

492
00:37:03,980 --> 00:37:10,820
Like, we choose, we pre-decide to learn from our trials because we know that afterwards, as we get out of those trials,

493
00:37:10,820 --> 00:37:15,380
we can come alongside other brothers and sisters and help them go through their trials.

494
00:37:15,380 --> 00:37:23,760
Spiritual maturity, learning through trials, is so important because it's an opportunity for us to help others.

495
00:37:25,180 --> 00:37:33,000
What great joy we can have in going through trials if we know that that trial can help us help other people.

496
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:36,400
It's another motivation for joy.

497
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:43,060
Not only are we going to get spiritual maturity out of it, but we're going to be able to help others who are going through it as well.

498
00:37:43,060 --> 00:37:48,120
The positive outcome of various trials is spiritual maturity.

499
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:53,360
Many of us are in the middle of various trials right now.

500
00:37:53,360 --> 00:38:03,080
Whether it's been brought on to you by your own decisions or the decisions of somebody else or just the effects of living in a fallen world.

501
00:38:03,080 --> 00:38:11,960
Maybe you've made godly decisions up until this point and you've chose joy and things are, at least you're learning from it, you're maturing through it.

502
00:38:12,900 --> 00:38:16,160
Maybe not so much, or maybe somewhere in between.

503
00:38:16,160 --> 00:38:23,100
I think the reality is, like, pre-deciding is a daily choice.

504
00:38:23,100 --> 00:38:28,360
Like, you don't just choose right at the beginning of your trial, I'm going to do this with joy.

505
00:38:28,360 --> 00:38:29,360
I'm going to mature through it.

506
00:38:29,360 --> 00:38:30,320
I'm going to grow through it.

507
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:32,420
God's going to use this trial in my life.

508
00:38:32,800 --> 00:38:35,500
And then, from then on, you never have to think about it again.

509
00:38:35,500 --> 00:38:42,420
Like, this is a daily decision in the midst of our trials to wake up and say, God, this is not what I would have chosen for my life.

510
00:38:42,420 --> 00:38:45,900
This is not where I would be if I could have designed the situation.

511
00:38:45,900 --> 00:38:51,760
But I'm going to choose to have joy in the midst of the situation because I know that you can use it for good.

512
00:38:51,760 --> 00:38:59,640
My encouragement to all of us facing trials is that we would wake up each day and pre-decide to view our trial with joy.

513
00:38:59,720 --> 00:39:01,980
Because we know that it can bring about spiritual maturity.

514
00:39:01,980 --> 00:39:05,800
Let's not waste an opportunity to become like Jesus.

515
00:39:05,800 --> 00:39:10,420
Let's not let bitterness and depression and anxiety grow in our hearts that lead us away from God.

516
00:39:10,420 --> 00:39:16,260
If you're here and you're not going through a difficult season,

517
00:39:16,260 --> 00:39:20,920
I just encourage you to look around your community and find the people that are

518
00:39:20,920 --> 00:39:24,780
and be the hands and feet of Jesus in their life.

519
00:39:24,780 --> 00:39:29,700
Like, choose to come alongside them and help them hold up their arms as they're struggling

520
00:39:29,700 --> 00:39:31,240
as they're suffering.

521
00:39:31,240 --> 00:39:35,340
We're going to take some meaning here in a minute.

522
00:39:35,340 --> 00:39:40,280
And I thought the best way for us to end would be to read that Hebrews passage.

523
00:39:40,280 --> 00:39:41,260
Hebrews chapter 4.

524
00:39:41,260 --> 00:39:44,260
I talked about Jesus being our great high priest.

525
00:39:44,260 --> 00:39:45,640
In Hebrews chapter 4 it says,

526
00:39:45,640 --> 00:39:52,520
So then, since we have a great high priest who has entered heaven,

527
00:39:52,520 --> 00:39:56,340
Jesus the Son of God, let us hold firmly to what we believe.

528
00:39:56,960 --> 00:40:00,580
This high priest of ours understands our weaknesses.

529
00:40:00,580 --> 00:40:03,920
For he has faced all of the same testings that we do.

530
00:40:03,920 --> 00:40:05,720
He's faced trial.

531
00:40:05,720 --> 00:40:06,680
He's faced tribulation.

532
00:40:06,680 --> 00:40:07,820
He's faced difficulty.

533
00:40:07,820 --> 00:40:09,660
Yet he chose not to sin.

534
00:40:09,660 --> 00:40:13,520
So let us come boldly to the throne of our gracious God.

535
00:40:13,520 --> 00:40:19,400
There we will receive his mercy and we will find his grace to help us when we need it most.

536
00:40:19,400 --> 00:40:26,120
When we go through trials, we go through trials not on our own,

537
00:40:26,120 --> 00:40:31,900
but inside the community of the church led by Jesus who is our high priest,

538
00:40:31,900 --> 00:40:35,020
who is the head of this thing we call the church.

539
00:40:35,020 --> 00:40:38,620
And he has been through every situation that you could ever imagine,

540
00:40:38,620 --> 00:40:40,920
the trials and the difficulties that you might be facing.

541
00:40:41,080 --> 00:40:46,480
Jesus faced them himself, and yet he chose not to sin.

542
00:40:46,480 --> 00:40:51,420
So when we're in those situations, we draw near to the throne of grace,

543
00:40:51,420 --> 00:40:55,200
receiving his grace, receiving his forgiveness.

544
00:40:55,200 --> 00:40:58,420
That's what communion is all about.

545
00:40:58,420 --> 00:41:00,000
That's why we take it every single week.

546
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:05,360
Because we remind ourselves that we're not at this thing alone.

547
00:41:05,360 --> 00:41:09,740
That we have a perfect example who is worthy of following.

548
00:41:09,740 --> 00:41:12,800
Who is worthy of suffering for.

549
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:16,360
Who is worthy of laying down our lives for.

550
00:41:16,360 --> 00:41:17,860
We choose to believe.

551
00:41:17,860 --> 00:41:21,940
The following Jesus is better than anything else.

552
00:41:21,940 --> 00:41:25,760
In the moments of trial, it might be easy to say,

553
00:41:25,760 --> 00:41:27,220
you know what, this is too hard.

554
00:41:28,020 --> 00:41:30,980
I'm going to just go do my own thing, live my own way.

555
00:41:30,980 --> 00:41:38,240
But God commands us to have no other gods before us,

556
00:41:38,240 --> 00:41:39,980
because, again, he knows they don't work.

557
00:41:39,980 --> 00:41:44,960
We can give up in the midst of trials and walk away from God.

558
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:48,480
There's no fulfillment and satisfaction in that.

559
00:41:48,480 --> 00:41:53,320
And so, if you're in here and you're a follower of Jesus,

560
00:41:54,520 --> 00:42:09,920
I would encourage you to take communion this morning remembering that we have a great high priest who in every way went before us and suffered in the same ways that we do and yet lived a perfect life, set a perfect example for us.

561
00:42:09,980 --> 00:42:16,600
Not so that we could be perfect because we can't, but so that when we fail, we draw near to his throne of grace.

562
00:42:16,600 --> 00:42:22,760
We receive his forgiveness because his body was broken for us and his blood was shed for us.

563
00:42:22,760 --> 00:42:28,300
If you consider yourself a follower of Jesus, let's take this morning the body of Christ broken for us.

564
00:42:28,300 --> 00:42:47,800
Man, my challenge for us is those of us who call Canvas home and come here on a regular basis.

565
00:42:49,140 --> 00:42:54,040
If we're not careful, communion can become just a thing that we do each week.

566
00:42:54,040 --> 00:43:03,740
Let's be a people that pre-decide, coming into communion each week, we pre-decide that we're going to let this thing do what it was meant to do.

567
00:43:03,740 --> 00:43:07,820
Like when Jesus set it up, he said, do this to remember me.

568
00:43:07,820 --> 00:43:10,300
Let's not just do this to check a box.

569
00:43:10,300 --> 00:43:14,500
Let's not just do this because it's the thing that we do as a community of believers.

570
00:43:14,500 --> 00:43:22,880
But let's do this to remember Jesus, our great high priest, who has gone before us, who has offered his blood as a sacrifice for our sins.

571
00:43:22,880 --> 00:43:27,620
Let's take the juice as a reminder of Christ's blood shed for us.

572
00:43:27,620 --> 00:43:42,540
Father, we thank you for this opportunity to begin to walk through the book of James.

573
00:43:43,980 --> 00:43:55,660
God, I pray ultimately that no matter where we are when it comes to trials, whether we're in the midst of various trials or we're on the other side of various trials,

574
00:43:55,660 --> 00:43:57,620
that we would choose to obey you.

575
00:43:57,620 --> 00:44:04,740
In the midst of our trials, that we would pre-decide to let it be an opportunity for us to become more like Jesus.

576
00:44:04,740 --> 00:44:13,080
On the other side of trials, that we would come alongside our brothers and sisters in Christ and help hold them up in the midst of their trials.

577
00:44:13,080 --> 00:44:20,120
God, let this be a season where we become more like you, whatever our circumstances might be.

578
00:44:20,120 --> 00:44:22,820
God, I'm thankful for this church.

579
00:44:22,820 --> 00:44:24,420
I'm thankful for the people here.

580
00:44:24,420 --> 00:44:30,620
I pray that we would learn to become more like you, for your glory and for our good.
